# StackRox UI Dev Server

When the user asks to start, run, or load the StackRox UI, use this setup:

## Start Command

Read the token from `.secrets/stackrox-api-token` and pass it as an env var:

```bash
CYPRESS_COMPONENT_TEST=true \
UI_START_TARGET=https://staging.demo.stackrox.com \
ROX_API_TOKEN="$(cat ../../.secrets/stackrox-api-token)" \
npm start
```

Run from `stackrox/ui/` (workspace root is `rhacs-ux-prototypes/`). The UI will be at `http://localhost:3000/`.

For offline prototypes, run `node stackrox/ui/apps/platform/mock-api.js` from the workspace root, then start the UI with `UI_START_TARGET=http://localhost:8444` instead of staging.

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `CYPRESS_COMPONENT_TEST=true` | Disables SSL so the dev server runs plain HTTP (avoids self-signed cert issues) |
| `UI_START_TARGET` | Proxy target for API requests — points to the staging Central instance |
| `ROX_API_TOKEN` | JWT API token injected into proxy headers and client-side localStorage for automatic auth |

## API Token Location

The token lives at the workspace root: `.secrets/stackrox-api-token` (gitignored). **NEVER** commit, push, or paste this token into tracked files, commits, PRs, or chat messages. If the token expires, generate a new one from the staging Central UI under Platform Configuration > Integrations > API Token and update the file.

## How Auth Works

Two things make auto-login work (both require `ROX_API_TOKEN`):

1. **Proxy-side**: `setupProxy.js` injects `Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED] on all proxied API requests
2. **Client-side**: `index.tsx` writes the token to `localStorage` (`access_token` key) on startup, so the auth saga sees the user as logged in

## Troubleshooting

- **Blank page / login screen**: Clear localStorage for `localhost:3000` in DevTools, then refresh
- **Port 3000 in use**: Kill stale processes with `lsof -ti :3000 | xargs kill -9`
- **API 403 errors**: The API token may have expired — generate a new one from the staging Central
